# Keep the serverless bundle to the read-only API and map.
#
# The root requirements.txt pulls rasterio, scipy and scikit-image for the SAR
# pipeline. Vercel's Python builder discovers requirements.txt by convention,
# so leaving it in the upload makes it a candidate for the function install —
# which either blows the 250 MB bundle limit or wins over the slim
# api/requirements.txt. Excluding it here leaves exactly one candidate.
#
# The leading slash matters: these patterns follow gitignore semantics, where
# a bare `requirements.txt` matches at EVERY level and would also exclude
# api/requirements.txt — which removes the only dependency manifest and makes
# Vercel stop recognising api/index.py as a function at all.
/requirements.txt
/requirements-dev.txt

# Not needed at runtime.
/tests/
/docs/
/scripts/
/db/
/data/
/.venv/
/Dockerfile
/docker-compose.yml
/pyproject.toml

# 1.6 MB of vendored Swagger UI; /docs degrades gracefully without it and the
# hosted deployment can reach a CDN anyway.
/frontend/vendor/swagger-ui/
